Third-party components
----------------------

The *source* in this repository is AGPL-3.0-only (relicensed from GPL-3.0-only
on 2026-09-26 by its sole copyright holder). The `package.sh` deploy build
compiles **no** vendor source and includes no vendor header: the ISP 3A/register
tier, the AAC encoder, the H.264 encoder, the VENC/ISP/capture middleware and the
daemon's own interface headers are all our clean-room code (the AGPL-3.0-only
`freewinner`/`freecodec` siblings); `libvenc_base.so` is built from that clean
source too. The SDK tree is still fetched at build time, but no vendor object
reaches the link — the table below is the audit trail for what it provides and
why nothing of it ships. (Notices are the result of an audit of the actual
archives, source headers and camera drivers.)

Userspace - CLOSED (no license grant) — **audited and NOT compiled into the
`package.sh` deploy build** (replaced by the clean-room tiers above):
* **Allwinner eyesee-mpp middleware** - `mpi_sys.c`, `mpi_vi.c`, `mpi_isp.c`,
  `mpi_venc.c`, `mpi_aenc.c`, the component / audio-HAL / vin glue and `libisp`
  (`isp.c`, `isp_tuning`, `isp_manage`, `isp_dev`, ...) are compiled from source
  supplied by the user's own Allwinner/Lindenis SDK tree
  (`repos/lindenis-v833-softwinner`, not redistributed here). Their headers carry
  `Copyright (C), 2001-2016/2018-2020, Allwinner Tech. Co., Ltd.` or
  `Copyright (c) 2016 by Allwinnertech Co., Ltd.` with **no license grant**.
  Replaced by our own `fcap_`/`fisp_`/`fenc_` packages and `mw_headers`; none of
  these vendor objects is linked into the deploy build, and none of these vendor
  headers is included by any translation unit in it. (The SDK `-I` roots remain
  on the compile command line for the legacy MPP TUs in non-deploy targets; in
  the deploy build they are unused.)
  `Clock_Component.c` / `tmessage.c`, and our SDK's copies of the libcedarc
  vencoder framework (`EncAdapter.c`, `FrameBufferManager.c`,
  `BitstreamManager.c`), carry an explicit proprietary notice ("confidential and
  proprietary ... only as expressly authorized by a licensing agreement from
  Softwinner Products").
  - Caveat on the vencoder framework: Allwinner has separately published the
    same CedarX encoder framework - `vencoder.c`, `EncAdapter.c`,
    `FrameBufferManager.c`, `BitstreamManager.c`, `venc_device.c` and
    `include/video_enc_reg.h` - under **LGPL-2.1-or-later** at
    github.com/allwinner-zh/media-codec (same author; our SDK copies are a later
    refactor). That framework is thus plausibly LGPL. The encoder *engine* is
    not: in that release too it is a closed binary plugin
    (`libcedar_plugin_venc.so`, repo allwinner-zh/media-codec-lib, no license),
    `dlopen`'d by `venc_device.c` and invoked via `CedarPluginVEncInit`. So the
    framework has LGPL provenance; the H.264 encoder core remains a blob.
* **Hardware H.264 encoder core** (`libvenc_codec.a/.so`, `libVE.a/.so`) - vendor
  binaries from the same SDK. Audited: they contain **no copyright line and no
  license text at all**. The `package.sh` deploy build links **none** of them: the
  H.264 engine is the clean-room `freecodec` implementation (static objects) and
  its framework is the clean-room `libvenc_base.so` built from
  `codec/src/base`. `package.sh` therefore ships no vendor encoder library.
  (The Makefile retains development targets that still use the vendor pair; they
  are not the deliverable.)
* **Prebuilt ISP 3A/tuning archives** (`libisp_ae/af/afs/awb/base/gtm/iso/md/
  pltm/rolloff.a`, or `libisp_algo_rtos.a`) - **replaced** in the deploy build by
  the AGPL-3.0-only clean-room `freewinner` tier; no 3A archive object is linked
  there (every member of the RTOS archive is dropped, leaving an empty archive).
  Only the opt-out vendor comparison builds (e.g. `ALGO_RTOS=` on the make
  command line) link them.
* **AAC**: the vendor `libaacenc.a` is **not** linked - replaced by our
  `freecodec` encoder (freewinner's `codec/`) over upstream **FAAC**
  (LGPL-2.1-or-later), fetched by `build.sh`. `libmp3enc.a` was never linked (mediad only selects
  AAC; the two MP3 entry points are stubbed). The clean-room `freewinner`/
  `freecodec` tiers are AGPL-3.0-only like this daemon, so the combined deploy
  binary is AGPL-3.0-only.

Kernel - OPEN (evidence: `.ko` modinfo on the camera):
* `vin_v4l2.ko` and `vin_io.ko` - "Dual BSD/GPL" (Allwinner); `cam_sensor.ko`
  - GPL; mainline `videobuf2-core/dma-contig/memops/v4l2.ko` - GPL. The camera's
  V4L2 nodes are `vin_video0..3`, `vin_cap.0..3`, `sunxi_isp.0/.1`,
  `sunxi_h3a.0/.1` (3A statistics), `sunxi_scaler`, `sunxi_csi`, `sunxi_mipi`.
* The Allwinner V4L2 UAPI header compiled via libisp
  (`include/V4l2Camera/linux/videodev2.h`) is GPL-2.0-or-later OR BSD-3-clause.
* The video-engine kernel driver (`cedar_ve`, `/dev/cedar_dev`, major 150) is
  built into the kernel image; its license was not extracted (mtd1 is
  compressed). The userspace encoder core over it is closed regardless.

Other:
* **alsa-lib** - `media_daemon/include/alsa/*.h` (19 headers, tracked in
  this repo): the public headers reached from `<alsa/asoundlib.h>`, from
  alsa-lib 1.1.4.1, LGPL-2.1-or-later. All are verbatim except `asoundlib.h`
  (`<sys/poll.h>` -> `<poll.h>` for musl, marked in the file). The camera's own
  `libasound.so.2` is linked at runtime, not redistributed.
* **rmm fshare ring format** - reverse engineered from the camera's own stock
  `rmm`; the stock binary is not redistributed.
* **Terminus Font** (bold, 8x16 and 16x32) - the glyph bitmaps in the
  generated `media_daemon/osd_font.h` are copied unmodified from Terminus
  4.49.1, Copyright (C) 2020 Dimitar Toshkov Zhekov, SIL Open Font License 1.1
  (Reserved Font Name "Terminus Font"). The licence is in
  `media_daemon/fonts/OFL-Terminus.txt` and must ship with the source and
  any distribution of the font data.
* **iniparser** (`libisp/iniparser`) - ships no license file in this SDK tree;
  upstream iniparser is MIT.


